# The ark: the generation ship, after the war on board. Built by
# `go run ./tools/mapgen -map ark`; this file is the level, and map.bin,
# map.json and the atlas beside them are what it compiles to. Add -leaks to
# prove the start is sealed.
#
# A cone standing on its point: the drive in the tip, eleven decks in the wide
# part of the cone, the drum and the ice dome on top as the heavy end. The ship
# coasts tumbling end over end about an axis through the drum, so "down" is
# away from the drum - towards the tip - on every deck, and the stars wheel past
# overhead. Gravity falls off towards the drum, which is the class system in one
# number: the servants live low and heavy, the elites high and light, with the
# most floor and the only windows.
#
#   y 170-182  ice dome        water ice: dust and radiation shield
#   y 149-170  drum R36        tanks, the AI core in the middle, 8 booms
#   y 146-148  D11 bridge      vented by the AI                     vacuum
#   y 141-145  D10 promenade   garden under glass, glass blown out  vacuum
#   y 137-140  D9  residences  four suites and an atrium, windows   vacuum
#   y 134-136  D8  staff flats officers and scientists, burnt       vacuum
#   y 130-133  D7  hydroponics blown open from outside              vacuum
#   ---------------------------- sealed: a hatch in the spine --------------
#   y 127-129  D6  medical     lab, gene vault, ward, cold storage  air  START
#   y 124-126  D5  crew flats  airlock east (+z), sealed            air
#   y 122-123  D4  service commons: mess, laundry, chapel, washrooms air
#   y 120-121  D3  service cabins, two metres to the ceiling        air
#   y 118-119  D2  service cabins                                   air
#   y 115-117  D1  life support: water tanks, airlock west, sealed  air
#   ---------------------------- sealed: a hatch in the spine --------------
#   y  28-114  lower cone      reaction mass round the spine        vacuum
#   y   0-27   drive           reactor, shadow shield, the bell (cold)
#
# A voxel is two metres (the player is 0.875 of one). The hull's radius is
# r(y) = 4 + (y-10)*26/140 from the tip at y=10 to the drum at y=149; every
# radius below is that line read at a height, so changing the cone means
# changing all of them. Ceilings go with class: one voxel on the service decks,
# two for crew and medical, three and four up where the money was.
#
# The spine is the one way between decks - a 3x3 shaft with a door on every
# deck, where a ladder goes - and two hatches in it close the six lower decks
# off from the rest; the airlocks are hatched shut too. Doors and ladders are
# props and are not placed yet, so a doorway here is a hole where one goes.

size 160 192 160
sky full
spin 10 axis=1,0,0
fog 200 900
ambient 0.55 0.60 0.75 0.30
ceiling 4 5 10
floor 4 5 10
music maintenance

# In the lab, facing its door.
spawn 88.5 128 70.5 dir=-1,0

# Air on D1-D6 and nowhere else: out to the outside of the hull, r(y), from
# D1's floor to D6's ceiling.
pressure 80.5 80.5 23.69 116 130 26.29

